.TH NEO-WEATHER 1 "2026-11-12" "gnome-phone 0.1.1" "GNOME Phone"
.SH NAME
neo-weather \- weather app for GNOME Phone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neo-weather
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the weather where the phone is: now, the next 24 hours, today against yesterday, the week and the details.
The place is a city chosen in the app (the location button: a search by name in Open-Meteo's geocoder, which works
with Location off, and which nothing moves afterwards; "Use my location" gives it up), otherwise the first city in
GNOME Weather if it has one, otherwise where GeoClue puts the phone (city accuracy), named by OpenStreetMap's
Nominatim. The forecast is Open-Meteo's (no key). The last place and forecast are kept in
.I ~/.cache/neo-launcher/
so the app opens on them at once.
.SH SEE ALSO
geoclue(5)
